[h1]🎉 Dome Keeper Mod Jam is Now LIVE! 🎉[/h1]

The wait is over, [b]the Dome Keeper Mod Jam has officially begun![/b] Time to unleash your creativity and bring your wildest ideas to life.

[h2]🔗 How to Get Started[/h2]
Before you dive in, make sure to:  
✅ [b]Register your team or solo entry on Discord[/b] – We’ve set up a dedicated forum for you to announce your participation. Head over to our [url=https://discord.gg/b6bM2zStrw]Discord server[/url] to get started.  
✅ [b]Get your own private channels[/b] – Once you’ve posted your team/solo entry, we’ll create a private chat and voice channel just for you! This ensures your team has a space to work, and our team can pop in to offer support when needed.  
✅ [b]Need support?[/b] Tag the [b]@Mod Jam Support[/b] role on Discord, and either [b]Jarvs, Ste, or Seraxis[/b] will assist you. Use your [b]private team chat[/b] for confidential matters or the [b]#mod-jam-general[/b] channel for public questions.  
✅ [b]Need art guidance?[/b] [b]Anne from Bippinbits[/b] is available to offer support.  


[h2]🛠️ Quick Rules Recap[/h2]

🏆 [b]Awards & Prizes:[/b] If you want your mod to be considered for an award, you must submit it via the [url=https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1aulrjxO4j2wXbxMa78AbZRoHhkAulSoGr1nGsZPP6AA/viewform?edit_requested=true]official submission form[/url] before the deadline.  

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40568463/b7259099e5160fad86b205629269564e181959c8.png[/img]

[b]🔹 Prizes:[/b]  
🥇 [b]Best Mod[/b] – $300 USD  
🥈 [b]Runner-Up[/b] – $200 USD  
🥉 [b]Second Runner-Up[/b] – $100 USD  
🏅 [b]Bonus Awards[/b] – Special categories may be announced!  

Each winner will also receive an [b]exclusive Dome Keeper Mod Jam hoodie[/b] and a [b]Drillbert plush toy[/b] for every team member ([b]max 6 per team[/b]).  

🎨 [b]AI Art Policy:[/b] We encourage original works and [b]will favour them during judging[/b]. AI-generated content can be used, but mods that rely heavily on AI art are [b]unlikely to win prizes[/b]. Programmer art is absolutely welcome!  

👥 [b]Team Size:[/b] Teams must have a maximum of [b]6 members[/b]. Prize money will need to be split by the team, so appointing a team leader to handle this is a good idea. Hoodies and plushies will be [b]capped at 6 per team.[/b]  

📜 [b]Full Rules & Policies:[/b] Please review our [url=https://github.com/DomeKeeperMods/Docs/wiki/Legal]updated EULA[/url], and [url=https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1aulrjxO4j2wXbxMa78AbZRoHhkAulSoGr1nGsZPP6AA/viewform?edit_requested=true]submission guidelines [/url], where you will find our other policies, before submitting your mod.  

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/40568463/fb33a7d0c2446cf5e365e6d9878ba015f6ae45ae.png[/img]

[h2]📅 Important Dates[/h2]

🛠️ [b]Mod Jam Duration:[/b] February 21st, 00:00 CET – February 28th, 23:00 CET  
📥 [b]Submission Deadline:[/b] February 28th, 23:00 CET  
🎤 [b]Award Show:[/b] One week after the event (exact date TBA)  

🚨 [b]Final Submission Requirements[/b] 🚨  
If you want to be [b]eligible for a prize[/b], your mod must be:  
✅ [b]Uploaded & tested[/b] on Steam Workshop  
✅ [b]Fully submitted[/b] via the [url=https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1aulrjxO4j2wXbxMa78AbZRoHhkAulSoGr1nGsZPP6AA/viewform?edit_requested=true]Official Submission Form[/url]  
✅ [b]Completed by 23:00 CET on Feb 28[/b]  
✅ [b]Once submitted, do not update until the winners are announced. Let us know before fixing any critical bugs.[/b]  


